{"metadata": {"version": "0.3.3", "copyright": "Copyright (c) 2026 graineo project; format and method by Andrea Volpato (spektrafilm). Licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0.", "created": "2026-10-28", "license": "spektrafilm profile by Andrea Volpato, licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0. Redistribution and derivatives must credit the author, link the project (https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm),preserve this license, and remain CC BY-SA 4.0.Modifications must be noted. Full text of the license and attribution requirements: https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm/blob/main/SPEKTRAFILM_LICENSE.txt.", "citation": "If you use this profile in your work, please cite the spektrafilm project: https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm, see CITATION.cff for details.", "datasource": "Characteristic curve (roll film, ILFORD ILFOTEC HC (1+31), 8 min, 20 C, intermittent agitation) and spectral sensitivity digitised from the Ilford data sheet (FP4 plus technical information, November 2018, pages 1 and 5). Original data are property of Harman technology Limited (Ilford). The data sheet gives relative log exposure only: the exposure axis was anchored so that the speed point (density = fog + 0.1) lies at log10(0.8/ISO 125) lux-s, and shifted by -0.94 log lux-s so that 0 is the mid-grey exposure at box speed. Sensitivity offset chosen so that mid-grey renders at the reference level; sensitivity is the sheet's relative (linear) wedge-spectrogram curve under tungsten light, used as given. Tail above the sheet range extrapolated with decaying slope. Single development time (the sheet shows one curve). ", "modifications": "New profile created from manufacturer data by the graineo project; only the profile format and wavelength grid taken from spektrafilm. grain_scale is an ESTIMATE (no data sheet value): target RMS granularity 9 assumed from the film class (similar to Kodak T-MAX / Tri-X class); simulated value at density 1.0 was 8.6 before scaling."}, "info": {"stock": "ilford_fp4_plus",